#: Game/Levels/Warmup/L01_NameWhatYouHave.lean:10
msgid "Name what you have"
msgstr ""

#. §0: `U`
#. §1: `V`
#. §2: `exact`
#. §3: `exact h`
#. §4: `h`
#: Game/Levels/Warmup/L01_NameWhatYouHave.lean:12
msgid "If you already know that §0 is contained in §1, you can say so. That is all this level asks.\n"
"\n"
"The real work here is on the right: the **inventory**. Every theorem listed there is one you met in the Set Theory Game. They are yours to use from now on; you will not be asked to prove them again.\n"
"\n"
"To finish a level you close every goal. When the goal is *exactly* one of your hypotheses, the tactic §2 closes it: §3 says \"the goal is §4\"."
msgstr ""

#. §0: $U \\subseteq V$
#. §1: $U \\subseteq V$
#: Game/Levels/Warmup/L01_NameWhatYouHave.lean:20
msgid "If §0, then §1."
msgstr ""

#: Game/Levels/Warmup/L01_NameWhatYouHave.lean:24
msgid "That is the whole move: recognise that what you need is already in your hands, and name it. Most levels in this game end by naming something you already have."
msgstr ""

#: Game/Levels/Warmup.lean:4
msgid "What You Already Know"
msgstr ""

#. §0: `exact`
#. §1: `intro`
#. §2: `apply`
#. §3: `rw`
#. §4: `obtain`
#. §5: `have`
#: Game/Levels/Warmup.lean:6
msgid "This world assumes you have played the **Set Theory Game** by Daniel Velleman.\n"
"\n"
"Nothing you proved there carries over automatically: each game on this server starts with an\n"
"empty inventory. So instead of asking you to prove those results again, this world *hands them\n"
"back* to you as tools, and then drills the moves you will need for topology: §0, §1,\n"
"§2, §3, §4, and §5, all on set membership.\n"
"\n"
"There is no boss level here. This world is an on-ramp."
msgstr ""

